=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ANALYSIS ===
Scenario: The counterexample shows that in the available system instance, even though Emergency mode is active and several requests are pending, the required scenario where at least one pending High, one pending Medium, and one pending Low classification request are all present in Emergency mode, and only the High-classification requests are processed in a single step, cannot be realized. In the concrete states, only requests of a single classification seem to be present or processed at each step, but the existential requirement for all three classification levels cannot be satisfied simultaneously given the allocation of users, roles, and request targets.
What went wrong: The assertion expects a transition in Emergency mode where all three classification levels are present among pending requests, and only the High requests are processed in one step, but the model instance cannot realize this scenario with the available resources and constraints.
Root cause: Ambiguous requirement / missing assumption — The requirements do not guarantee that every instance contains requests at all three classification levels in Emergency mode unless explicit enabling facts are provided in the scenario predicate.
Fix: Add explicit enabling facts in the EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario predicate (e.g., require that there exists at least one request at High, Medium, and Low classification assigned to different objects/users, with sufficient clearance and object classification), or clarify the requirement to state whether this scenario must always be possible or only in certain scenario runs.
