What went wrong: The model instance fails to satisfy the enabling assumptions for the scenario (no state with pending requests at all three classification levels in Emergency mode), so the assertion fails not due to a model error, but because the universal assertion is stronger than the model guarantees.

Root cause: Ambiguous requirement / missing assumption—lack of a system-wide coverage fact for request classification means the group-processing scenario may not be possible in every instance, so the assertion is only valid in scenario runs with explicit enabling assumptions.

Fix: Restrict the assertion to scenario runs/predicates where the enabling assumptions are guaranteed; do not require the scenario as a universal property unless the requirements are changed to require global coverage of request classifications.
